<%# The request's CSP nonce, for the one inline script left in this head and
    for javascript_import_module_tag below (importmap-rails nonces its own tags).
    nil when the host sets no nonce generator, and then no attribute renders. %>
<% studio_script_nonce = (content_security_policy_nonce if respond_to?(:content_security_policy_nonce)) %>
<%# PRE-PAINT THEME. Inline, and the only inline script this head keeps: it adds
    `dark` before the first paint, which no deferred module can do. The toggle
    lives in studio/alpine_stores. %>
<%= tag.script(nonce: studio_script_nonce) do %>
  (function(){
    if (localStorage.getItem('theme') !== 'light') {
      document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');
    }
  })();
<% end %>

<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<%# Studio.nav_spinner_min_ms, read by the nav spinner in studio/head_chrome. %>
<meta name="studio-nav-spinner-min-ms" content="<%= Studio.nav_spinner_min_ms.to_i %>">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<%= csrf_meta_tags %>
<%= csp_meta_tag %>
<%# The session-drift stamp + browser store. Renders nothing unless the controller
    includes Studio::ErrorHandling. See studio/_session_stamp. %>
<%= render "studio/session_stamp" %>
<%= render "layouts/studio/smooth_load" %>
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png">
<%# Link-preview (og:/twitter:) tags: the page's link_preview override, else the
    operator default from /admin/link_preview, else the static fallback. Gated by
    Studio.link_preview_tags? — under the default :auto, only once this app has
    installed the studio_site_identities table, so an app that emits its
    own tags gets no second set. See docs/LINK_PREVIEW.md. %>
<%= studio_link_preview_tags if respond_to?(:studio_link_preview_tags) && Studio.link_preview_tags? %>

<%= yield :head %>

<%= studio_theme_css_tag %>

<%# Montserrat is VENDORED into the engine (studio/montserrat-latin.woff2 and
    studio/montserrat-latin-ext.woff2) and shipped through the asset pipeline, no CDN,
    CSP-safe (same-origin :self), mirroring alpine, canvas_confetti and sortable below.
    PINNED AT Google Fonts v31.

    WHAT THIS REPLACED, and why it was never merely a third-party tidy-up:

      <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
      <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
      <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@...&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    The STYLESHEET blocks the load event. The font FILES it names do not. So the page
    went interactive in the fallback font and every glyph was re-measured when
    Montserrat landed a moment later. Root-caused in close-board-filter-flake: the
    board filter chips changed width AFTER the page was interactive, a synthesized
    click had its pointerdown and pointerup land on different elements, and the browser
    fired click on their COMMON ANCESTOR, so the toggle never ran. Three CI reds in one
    day (chip found at 45ms, clicked at 68ms). click_when_settled now guards the TEST
    lane; it does nothing for a real finger on a cold cache, which is what this removes.

    font-display: optional, NOT swap, and that is the substance of the fix.
    swap has an UNBOUNDED swap period, so a late font always reflows — self-hosting
    shortens that window but cannot close it. optional gives the browser a block period
    of about 100ms and NO swap period: if the file is not ready in time the page keeps
    the fallback for that navigation and never swaps. The reflow is not shortened, it is
    removed, and removed by construction rather than by being fast enough. block and
    fallback both retain a swap window and so retain the defect. THE COST, NAMED: a
    first visit on a slow link can render one page in system-ui. The preload below is
    what makes that rare, and the file is in the HTTP cache for every navigation after.

    WHY crossorigin ON A PRELOAD OF OUR OWN FILE. Fonts are fetched in CORS mode
    whatever their origin, so a preload without crossorigin does not match the request
    the font-face makes and the browser fetches the file TWICE. Only latin is
    preloaded: latin-ext is 68KB that most pages never render a glyph from.

    LATIN AND LATIN-EXT ONLY, measured rather than copied across. The old link pulled
    five subsets. cyrillic, cyrillic-ext and vietnamese occur ZERO times in the engine
    views, in all three consumers views, and in their seed, fixture and locale data.
    latin-ext earns its place on real rendered content: turf-monster seeds roster names
    including Modric, Kovacic, Gvardiol, Dzeko, Calhanoglu, Yildiz and Soucek. Dropping
    the three unused subsets keeps 56KB out of the gem, and unicode-range means a page
    only ever downloads the subsets it actually renders — so keeping latin-ext costs an
    English page nothing at all.

    ONE FILE PER SUBSET COVERS EVERY WEIGHT. Montserrat v31 is a VARIABLE font, which
    the six-weight link obscured: 400, 500, 600, 700, 800 and 900 all resolved to the
    SAME bytes. Verified by fetching them and reading the fvar table, not assumed. So
    each face below declares the whole 100-900 axis instead of six static instances.
    Asking for fewer weights would not have saved a byte, and every weight the fleet
    uses (measured: 400, 500, 600, 700, 800 as utilities, 900 in level-badge-10 and the
    theme-settings specimen) renders from real outlines rather than a synthesized fake. %>
<link rel="preload" href="<%= asset_path("studio/montserrat-latin.woff2") %>" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Montserrat';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-display: optional;
    src: url('<%= asset_path("studio/montserrat-latin.woff2") %>') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Montserrat';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-display: optional;
    src: url('<%= asset_path("studio/montserrat-latin-ext.woff2") %>') format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C0, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;
  }
</style>

<%# canvas-confetti is VENDORED into the engine (studio/canvas_confetti.js) and
    shipped through the asset pipeline — no CDN, CSP-safe (same-origin :self),
    zero-per-app dependency. Defines the global `confetti`; studio_confetti.js
    then builds window.studioConfetti (burst/cannons). fireSuccessConfetti
    (studio/head_chrome) rides the same global. %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "studio/canvas_confetti", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "studio/studio_confetti", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%# SortableJS is VENDORED into the engine (studio/sortable.js) and shipped through
    the asset pipeline — no CDN, CSP-safe (same-origin :self). Defines the global
    `Sortable`; the studio/board primitive (studio/_board_assets -> window.studioBoard)
    drives it for drag-reorder kanban AND depth-chart boards. Loaded here (deferred)
    so any board consumer has it with zero per-app wiring, mirroring canvas_confetti. %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "studio/sortable", defer: true, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%# The theme and devMode stores are studio/alpine_stores (its module tag is below).
    showNavSpinner / hideNavSpinner and fireSuccessConfetti are studio/head_chrome,
    installed by studio/alpine_shims. %>

<style>
  /* studio-engine: a sticky navbar that shrinks on scroll changes layout
     above the fold — Chrome/Firefox scroll-anchoring then compensates by
     moving scrollY, which re-crosses the collapse threshold and bounces.
     Disabling anchoring document-wide stops scrollY being dragged by the
     navbar resize. */
  body { overflow-anchor: none; }
</style>
<%# THE PINNED STACK: studio/pinned_stack publishes --pin-<name>-h, -bottom and
    -top for every [data-pin] layer, --pin-stack-bottom, and the legacy --nav-h /
    --nav-bottom. Started by studio/application. %>

<style>
  /* studio-engine: --nav-p, the sticky header's COLLAPSE PROGRESS, 0 (expanded)
     to 1 (collapsed). Third of the header properties published from this file,
     and the only one that is an INPUT to the header rather than a measurement
     of it — --nav-h and --nav-bottom above say how big it is, this says how far
     through its collapse it has got.

     REGISTERED, not merely declared. Untyped, `calc(3rem - 1rem * var(--nav-p))`
     is invalid at computed-value time on a page that has never scrolled and
     every collapsing dimension drops to its unstyled default; the <number> type
     is what makes the arithmetic legal and the initial value real. Registration
     also makes it INTERPOLABLE, which is how /navbar's Scrolled toggle animates
     the whole collapse by transitioning one property. */
  @property --nav-p {
    syntax: "<number>";
    inherits: true;
    initial-value: 0;
  }
</style>
<%# The collapse itself is studio/nav_collapse, bound by the engine's nav-collapse
    controller (and by the navCollapse() Alpine shim for headers that still say
    x-data="navCollapse()"). %>

<%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% if Studio.sticky_table_headers %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "studio/sticky_table_header", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% end %>
<%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
<%# THE ENGINE'S BROWSER BOOT (studio/application): its Stimulus application,
    the pinned stack, and the Alpine shims. A module tag, so it carries the nonce. %>
<%= javascript_import_module_tag "studio/application" %>
<%# THE STORES, BY THEIR OWN DOOR. Every host's <body> binds $store.devMode and the
    theme toggle binds $store.theme, so a boot that fails to load (a missing digest,
    a network drop, a throw anywhere in its graph) must not take the stores with it.
    studio/alpine_stores imports nothing and installs them on alpine:init; it is
    also in the boot graph, so this resolves to the same preloaded module and
    registers nothing twice. A module tag, so it carries the nonce: never a bare
    inline fallback (e2e/stores_survive_boot_failure.spec.js). %>
<%= javascript_import_module_tag "studio/alpine_stores" %>
<%# THE MODAL STACK, BY ITS OWN DOOR, for the same reason. studio/modal_host
    registers $store.modals (and each page-scoped host's store) on alpine:init and
    publishes window.ModalAnimations and window.StudioModals; a host's template
    binds $store.modals.current(), so a failed boot must not take the store with
    it. It imports nothing, and the modal-host controller imports it, so this
    resolves to the same preloaded module. %>
<%= javascript_import_module_tag "studio/modal_host" %>
<%# THE TOAST QUEUE, BY ITS OWN DOOR, for the same reason. studio/toast registers
    $store.toasts on alpine:init, listens for the `toast` window event and seeds
    the flash layouts/studio/_flash renders, so a failed boot leaves a page its
    flash and its toasts. It imports nothing, and the toast controller imports it. %>
<%= javascript_import_module_tag "studio/toast" %>
<%# ALPINE LOADS AFTER THE MODULE TAGS, and the order is the contract. Deferred
    classic scripts and module scripts execute in document order, so by the time
    Alpine starts, studio/application has defined the shims it evaluates
    (x-data="navCollapse()"), studio/alpine_stores has registered the
    `alpine:init` listener that installs $store.theme and $store.devMode, and
    studio/modal_host the one that installs each modal host's store. Moved
    above the module tags, Alpine would evaluate those before they exist (e2e/stimulus_boot.spec.js). %>
<%# Alpine is VENDORED into the engine (studio/alpine.js) and shipped through the
    asset pipeline — no CDN, CSP-safe (same-origin :self), mirroring canvas_confetti
    and sortable below. PINNED AT 3.16.1.

    WHAT THIS REPLACED, and why it is worth the 47KB in the repo: the tag here was

      <script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/alpinejs@3.x.x/dist/cdn.min.js">

    — a FLOATING major range, fetched from a third party at page load, for the
    library every chip, drawer, modal and board filter in the fleet depends on.
    Three consequences, none of them visible in a diff: two CI runs on ONE SHA could
    execute different Alpine builds; production interactivity depended on jsDelivr
    being reachable and honest; and an upgrade arrived with no review, because
    nothing changed in the repo when it did. Bumping is now a deliberate act —
    replace the file, change the version in this comment, and the diff shows it.

    Investigated as a suspect in the board-filter flake (three PRs reddened in one
    day, 2026-08-15). This removes a real source of run-to-run variance; it does NOT
    claim to be that flake's cause, and the remaining suspect there is untouched. %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "studio/alpine", defer: true, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% if Studio.sticky_table_headers %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag "studio/sticky_table_header", defer: true, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% end %>
